    required content and AGENTS.md is held to pointer length.
  - AC-40: exactly two production project references, checked at both the
    declared and the compiled level.
  - AC-41: no TaxCases in the project file, in the assembly's references, or in
    any executable line of the module; and no reverse reference to CaseProcessing
    from TaxLogicEngine, TaxCases, DocumentExtraction, or any of their three test
    trees (project files and handwritten sources both scanned).
  - AC-42: no DateTime.Now/UtcNow, Stopwatch, or TimeProvider; no filesystem,
    network, database/ORM, environment or current-user access; no
    OCR/LLM/cloud/email token; no ASP.NET Core; no generated identifier.
  - Also: no CRA line-number literal (any five-digit run), no box→line table
    (T4LineMappingConfig, T4BoxLineMapping, T4LineMap.Create, Dictionary<,
    T4BoxCodes, T4OtherInformationCodes), no TaxLogicEngine.Mappings resource
    read, no MoneyRounding / Math.Round / MidpointRounding / double / float /
    decimal, no SafeDiagnosticText or other masking helper, no
    RecipientIdentifier construction, no SIN property or SIN type on any module
    type, and no T5 token.
Design notes for review:
  - Scans read executable lines only. This module's documentation legitimately
    names nearly every forbidden concept while explaining why it is forbidden, so
    scanning raw text would make honest comments unwritable.
  - The year scan looks for any four-digit year rather than the literal 2025, so
    hardcoding a different year outside the policy type also trips it.
  - The production file set is pinned by exact file name rather than by a count,
    so a renamed or added production file is visible rather than silently
    unscanned.
Scanner guards (most assertions here are absence claims a broken walk would
satisfy for free):
  - TheScanner_SeesEveryProductionFileAndStillMatchesAKnownPattern pins the exact
    five-file production set by name, requires >2000 chars of executable source,
    and requires known-present patterns (T4SlipParser, IT4LineMapProvider) to
    still match.
  - TheCommentFilter_RemovesDocumentationWithoutRemovingCode proves the filter
    works in both directions on a real file: PayloadStructureGuard.cs documents
    T4RawBox.Value, the filter removes it, and IsNullOrWhiteSpace survives.
Mutation evidence (every arm was driven by a real violation):
  - Read DateTime.UtcNow in the processor -> 1 test fails.
  - Name TaxCases in production source (as a string literal) -> 1 test fails.
  - Hardcode a CRA-shaped literal "12100" -> 2 tests fail.
  - Hardcode 2025 outside SupportedProcessingTaxYears -> 1 test fails.
  - Add a Dictionary<string, string> (a second mapping authority) -> 1 test fails.
  - Reverse reference: a TaxLogicEngine source file mentions CaseProcessing ->
    1 test fails.
  - Add a PackageReference to CaseProcessing.csproj -> 1 test fails.
  - Add a third production project reference (TaxCases) -> 2 tests fail.
  - Note: nameof(TaxCases) in production source does not compile at all, because
    the reference does not exist. The boundary is compiler-enforced for types;
    the source scan catches what the compiler cannot see, such as a string
    literal.
